🔐 Backend Authentication & Role-Based Access System

This project is a backend application built using Node.js, Express, and MongoDB that implements secure JWT authentication and role-based access control (RBAC).

The system allows users to register, log in, and access different routes based on their assigned roles such as Admin, Teacher, and Student.

🚀 Key Features
User Registration with role selection
Secure Login using JWT (JSON Web Token)
Password hashing using bcrypt
Protected routes using middleware
Role-based authorization (Admin / Teacher / Student)
Clean and modular backend structure
Tested using Thunder Client / Postman
🛠️ Tech Stack
Backend: Node.js, Express.js
Database: MongoDB (Mongoose)
Authentication: JWT
Security: bcrypt
📁 Project Structure
backend/
│── config/
│   └── db.js
│── controllers/
│   └── authController.js
│── middleware/
│   ├── authMiddleware.js
│   └── roleMiddleware.js
│── models/
│   └── User.js
│── routes/
│   ├── authRoutes.js
│   └── protectedRoutes.js
│── .env
│── server.js
🔐 How Authentication Works
User registers with name, email, password, and role
Password is hashed before storing in database
On login, a JWT token is generated

Token is sent in request headers:

Authorization: Bearer <token>
Middleware verifies token and extracts user info
Role middleware checks if user has permission
📡 API Endpoints
🔹 Authentication
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/auth/register	Register new user
POST	/api/auth/login	Login and get token
🔹 Protected Routes
Method	Endpoint	Access
GET	/api/dashboard	All logged-in users
GET	/api/admin	Admin & Super Admin
GET	/api/teacher	Teacher only
GET	/api/student	Student only
🧪 Example Login Request
POST /api/auth/login
{
  "email": "teacher@gmail.com",
  "password": "123456"
}
📸 API Testing (Dashboard Access)




⚙️ Setup Instructions
Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/hu17-m/backend-auth-system.git
Install dependencies
npm install
Create .env file
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_url
JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key
Run the server
npx nodemon server.js
